(BAS-30 - the error-handler example, LANGUAGE.md:105:
 `On error print "Something went wrong", exit 1.`
 Both actions belong to the handler, so the exit fires and `Print "not
 reached"` never runs. The handler binds to the statement BEFORE it - the
 out-of-bounds byte read - which is what raises the flag.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-30.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Something went wrong
   (exit 1)
)
a buffer called small is 4 bytes in size.
a number called stray is byte 99 of small.
On error print "Something went wrong", exit 1.
Print "not reached".
